title: Payers › Header › What the header says
route: /payers/:id
intro: The card above the tabs. It names the payer, carries one quiet label that says its rules are demo data, and says what a coordinator needs first: plan type, programs, whether an initial request or a continued-stay review is needed, notice and how the payer is reached, and the policy status. Everything is read from the payer and its saved configuration. Approved as asked and typical decision are no longer here: Analytics shows them.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Pick a payer\n(or arrive on Payers)"
screen head "Payer header\nPayer name in large type\n'Edit log' and 'Edit' on the right\nThe demo-rules label under the name\nPlan line under that"

group gF "Four rows under the name"
  screen f1 "'Plan type'\n'Medicaid managed care (HMO). Claims go to Summit, not to the state.'\nNothing is shown when the payer has no plan type"
  screen f2 "'Programs'\nResidential 3.5, IOP, PHP, Detox\nor the ones chosen when the payer was added"
  screen f3 "'Needs'\n'Initial request: required. Notice within 24 hours of admission.'\n'Continued-stay review: required. A continued-stay review every 7 days after the first 7.'"
  screen f4 "'Notice and reach'\n'Notice due 24 hours after admission.'\n'Reached by portal, phone as backup.'"
endgroup

process cfg "Plan type, programs and needs are read from the saved configuration\nEdit a rule, a document list or the workflow and the header follows"
process pt "Plan type: the payer's group and the plan type New case would pre-fill\nSee 'Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Plan type and routing'"
decision ndn "Does the saved 'Submission windows' rule\nstill have a notice line\nand a continued-stay line?"
process need1 "Both read 'required' with the rule's own words"
process need2 "A missing line reads 'not on file'\nThe row in the payer list says 'Initial only' or 'Review only'"
process cfg2 "'Notice due' and 'Reached by' come from the payer's saved details\nthe 'Edit' button changes them"
goto g_ps "Continues in: Payers › Header › Policy status and the demo-rules label"

decision logn "Any edits logged for this payer?"
screen logb1 "Button reads 'Edit log (3)'\nthe count is edits for this payer"
screen logb0 "Button reads 'Edit log'"
click ce "Click 'Edit'"
click cl "Click 'Edit log'"
goto g_edit "Continues in: Payers › Edit payer details"
goto g_log "Continues in: Payers › Edit log"
end e1 "Header shows the payer's current state"

s1 --> head --> f1 & f2 & f3 & f4
f1 -.-> pt
f1 & f2 & f3 -.-> cfg
f3 --> ndn
ndn -->|Yes| need1 --> logn
ndn -->|No| need2 --> logn
f4 -.-> cfg2
head --> g_ps
logn -->|Yes| logb1 --> e1
logn -->|No| logb0 --> e1
head --> ce --> g_edit
head --> cl --> g_log
